<%#
  ONE ROW'S TILE — thumbnail + name. Extracted from _attachment_group.html.erb (stage 3, S3-1) so
  _file_tree_section.html.erb and the folder panels can render the identical tile without a second copy of the
  thumb_cell_data/file_menu_data wire contract (docs/invariants/files-preview.md).

  Local: row (Maker::ProjectFolderListing::Row). Reads @project, @addon_origins and @page_thumbs
  off the enclosing template — exactly as the block this was extracted from always did — because
  every caller on this page already builds those three the same way, over the same tile_ids union.

  THE TILE OPENS THE FILE (file_path), like Photos, Schematics and the hero beside it: a click
  opens it and a double-click opens it in a new tab (FilesHelper#file_open_data, 2026-10-21). It
  once opened the file's folder in the Library with the file selected (slice 6); a click that
  lands somewhere other than the thing clicked read as a detour, so the owner asked for it to just
  open (2026-10-20). This tile is NOT a selection item — nothing here goes through with_selection,
  because this page has no selection controller. The file menu's Open follows this href, and its
  Details lands in the Library with the file's side panel open.

  Optional local `notes` ({ node_id => sentence }, projects/_attachment_group): one muted line under
  the name, OUTSIDE the link, so it reads as a fact about the file rather than part of its name.
%>
<% node = row.node %>
<% ext = File.extname(node.name).delete(".").upcase.first(4) %>
<% note = local_assigns.fetch(:notes, {})[row.node_id] %>
<div class="attachment-tile">
  <%= link_to file_path(row.node_id), class: "grid-card file-cell",
              data: file_open_data(thumb_cell_data(row.node_id, ext)
                                     .merge(file_menu_data(node, @addon_origins[row.node_id]))) do %>
    <%= render "files/thumb", thumb: @page_thumbs.thumb(row.node_id), ext_label: ext,
               url: preview_src(@page_thumbs.thumb(row.node_id)) %>
    <span class="grid-name"><%= node.name %></span>
  <% end %>
  <% if note %><p class="tile-note muted"><%= note %></p><% end %>
  <%# A STACK'S MEMBER SAYS WHICH IT IS and can leave the stack; a file pulled out of its stack offers
      to go back, quietly (Shop manual spec §9). `member` is the role, "latest" or "older", given by
      projects/_stack_tile; @stacks is ProjectsController#show's. %>
  <% if (member = local_assigns[:member]) %>
    <span class="stack-role"><%= member %></span>
    <%= button_to "Pull out", file_stack_exclusion_path(row.node_id), method: :post, class: "linkbtn stack-pull-out",
                  form_class: "stack-pull-out-form", aria: { label: "Pull #{node.name} out of its stack" } %>
  <% elsif @stacks&.pulled_out?(row.node_id) %>
    <%= button_to "Put back", file_stack_exclusion_path(row.node_id), method: :delete, class: "linkbtn stack-put-back",
                  form_class: "stack-put-back-form", aria: { label: "Put #{node.name} back in its stack" } %>
  <% end %>
</div>
